{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_regk2wivnqfggceqtdg36jwb3ydwkpnyhv3nod5qgnjwkgkyfp5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte in every configuration.\n\n**Result: no divergences found. `translation/src/lib.rs` needed no fixes.**\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff (C minus Rust) | **empty**; all 3 symbols exported, `dlsym`-resolvable, no unresolved non-libc symbols |\n| Phase B — all 30 `CONFIGS.md` rows | 28 tests pass (randomized, fixed seed) |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `add_executable` / `[[bin]]`; stdout compared around FFI calls instead |\n| Phase C — all 13 `ERRORS.md` rows | 15 tests pass, asserting exact codes (`-1`/`-2`/NULL), not \"both failed\" |\n| Every feature combo | `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; `{default, --no-default-features}` × `{dev, release}` = 4 configs, all pass |\n\n**Deliverables in `translation/`:** `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `verify_all.sh`, and `tests/{common/mod.rs, phase_b_valid_paths.rs, phase_c_error_paths.rs, phase_d_symbols.rs}`. `c_src/` unmodified (only `c_src/build/` added).\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **I proved the harness is actually sensitive.** \"All green\" is worthless if the tests can't see a bug, so I injected 6 deliberate mutations (`x*2`→`x*3`, `x<0`→`x<=0`, fgets size 100→99, `-2`→`-3`, an error-string typo, `ferror != 0`→`== 0`) and confirmed each was caught (14–28 failures). During that check my backup file was lost to a `$TMPDIR` rotation and mutations accumulated in `src/lib.rs`; I reverted all 6 sites and confirmed the file is **byte-identical** to the original via `diff` against an independently reconstructed copy.\n\n2. **The first test run had 7 failures that were harness bugs, not translation bugs** — libtest's own `test foo ... ok` progress output was leaking into my `dup2` fd-1 capture from parallel threads. Fixed by flushing Rust's `stdout`/`stderr` alongside `fflush(NULL)` and pinning `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1`. I did not touch the C or the Rust library for this.\n\nThe translation correctly replicates several things that look like bugs but are the C's real behavior: two's-complement wrap on the UB `x * 2` overflow, the `-1` return colliding with the error sentinel, `printf(\"%s\")` truncating at embedded NULs, and `fopen` succeeding on a directory so failure only surfaces at the later `ferror` check (the one path where `fclose` runs during cleanup). These are documented in `VERIFICATION.md` so they aren't mistaken for defects later."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1995,"cache_read_input_tokens":108518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1995,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628cc379-0a70-404c-8e98-1f991b8a1c5b","uuid":"ed999886-bb5c-4373-b300-6e7320181fae","timestamp":"2026-09-05T14:29:15.245Z"}
